        "message": "LU-20076 tests: commit OST destroys when waiting for them\n\nwait_delete_completed_mds() polls until the MDT has heard that\nthe OSTs committed its destroys. force_sync on the MDT sends\nthem at once, but the OST commits them on its own schedule, up\nto 5 seconds later, and the OSP hears of that only from the\nreply to its next ping, up to 5 seconds after that. Each wait\ntakes 4 to 8 seconds, and sanity-quota makes over 300 of them per\nrun, sanity about 65.\n\nAt 300 waits in sanity-quota and 65 in sanity, the 4 to 8 second\ndelay accounts for about 20 to 40 minutes and 4 to 9 minutes per\nfull suite run, respectively, or 24 to 49 minutes combined. This\nis the estimated removable polling delay, not a measured end-to-end\nsaving: OST sync and ping costs and the statfs wait below reduce it.\n\nSync the OSTs and ping them from the MDTs before polling, so the\nOSPs learn of the commit at once. Syncing the OSTs alone does\nnot help, since the OSP still waits for its next ping.\n\nsanity 64d fills OST0000, and 64e and 64f then failed when they\nstarted before the MDT's cached statfs for the OST had refreshed:\ntheir stripe went to OST0001. They only passed because the old\nwait took longer than the refresh, so wait for it in 64d.\n\nThis wait used to take long enough to hide another delay. Since\nLU-18938 objects are freed by a background job about once a\nsecond, after the destroy has committed and every counter reads\n0, so quota tests on a fast host saw deleted files still charged.\nHave force_sync run that job, as the target sync paths already\ndo, and sync the OSTs once more when the wait ends. That adds\nabout 0.02 seconds to a wait.\n\nWith this series on a fast node, 5 of 12 runs of sanity-quota 1a,\n1b, 1d, 1h, 1i, 3a and 3b failed before this and 63 of 63 pass.\n\nFixes: 444d29c21891 (\"LU-18938 obdclass: delay an object free\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-quota fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=\"1a 1b 1d 1h 1i 3a 3b\",ONLY_REPEAT=9\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I2aa33483e64f56eef563122b53a333b65e24f1ac\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
